waiver: harness-limit
reason: internal/interp has no bump allocator — it is a tree-walking
  evaluator over Go values — so __heap_bump_bytes() returns 0 there
  unconditionally and the shape this case measures is unobservable.
  Giving the interpreter a fake arena would make it report numbers that
  describe nothing; see docs/ALLOCATION-OBSERVABLE.md. The wasm leg was
  excluded too until #6423 — it never reclaimed a heap string — and is
  back now that it does.
